Overview

    'Immortal Engine' <(working title)> is a free, open-source application for playing, sharing, and creating 
    VTTs <(Virtual Tabletops)> for any TTRPG <(Tabletop Roleplaying Game)>. We believe that TTRPGs should 
    be accessible to everyone, and in the digital age this has never been easier. However, many facets of 
    the TTRPG experience — NPCs, combat order, ability, GM tools, etc. — have been stuck 
    firmly in <'pen and paper'>… until now!

    The 'Immortal Engine' allows for the digital implementation of quite literally, any TTRPG feature!
    We believe the TTRPG Space has always been carried by its community: from Local Game Stores, to
    crowd-funding, and even simply getting a group of friends together to form your first party.
    As such, our app is centred wholly around this philosophy.

    Our 'Immortal Editor' <(working title)> allows Creators to model new or existing TTRPG systems
    using a purpose-built modelling/scripting language (that is fully {{{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turing_completeness}Turing Complete}}).
    These created 'model packages' can be shared online directly or using the app's built-in repository.
    Players can then install these packages and run them through the Engine. 

    For example, you could create a fully interactive Virtual Character Sheet that links to a party of other
    players and a GM, that <also> links to a Battle Map! The Sky truly is the limit, all you need to do is 
    download the model or build it yourself!

    If you wish to install the latest version of the project, please refer to {{{https://github.com/KLSumEd/Immortal-Editor}the GitHub Repository}}.